<title>BELARUS: Belarus president appoints privatisation minister.</title>
<headline>Belarus president appoints privatisation minister.</headline>
<dateline>MINSK 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belarus's president, Alexander Lukashenko, has appointed Vasily Novak minister of privatisation and state property, filling a post which had been vacant for over a year, the president's press office said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Novak, 41, a former chairman of a collective farm, previously worked in the president's office.</p>
<p>International financial organisations have criticised Belarus for its slow progress on privatisation.</p>
</text>
